{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>What, my son</b> — its meaning: what are you considered a ברי and a בן בטני, since I gave birth to you." "<b>My vows</b> — that I vowed at the time of my giving birth to you: if I escape the travail of childbirth, therefore I chastised you that you not give your strength to women, and do not give your ways to efface the ways of kings, that is, let not your practice be to deviate from the practice of kings, for harlotry and the drinking of wine and strong drink do not befit them, lest each one of them drink and forget what was expounded as law upon the book."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "The phrase ואל תתן דרכיך למחות דרכי המלכים is rendered hyper-literally; the syntax is compressed and the sense of למחות here is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:48.087059659Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}